{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"TWO MORE CLOSE REFUSALS, BOTH CORRECT AND BOTH MINE.\n2507 and 2510 went fully green (LLM +1, Verified +1), so 0880 and 9ca8 became closeable — and the\nclose gate refused both for SCOPE DRIFT:\n  0880: the commit changes reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.json and\n        scripts/_backtest/{__init__,all_work,stats}.py, none of which the recorded file_impact\n        declared. The extraction into a subpackage was a real design decision made during\n        implementation and I never widened the plan to match.\n  9ca8: same shape — the shipped commit adds scripts/_mechanism_delta/markers.py (a fifth helper the\n        implementer justified), AGENTS.md and docs/architecture.md, none declared.\nThe gate's wording is the right frame: 'the work went beyond the reviewed plan'. That is exactly what\nhappened, and it is the kind of drift a plan-review gate exists to notice.\nWidened both file_impacts to match what the commits actually touch — 11 paths for 0880, 13 for 9ca8,\neach with a reason. Widening is a MATERIAL change, so it invalidates the attestation by design;\nre-reviews started for both, plus f9b9 (still stale-material from its AC3 rewording).\nThree reviews running in parallel. They are bounded workloads that terminate with a verdict, which is\nwhy AGENTS.md carves gate runs out of the process-bounding rule — but I will confirm they exit rather\nthan assume it.\n\nCLOSED: 8ce5. GREEN AND AWAITING RE-REVIEW: 0880 (2507), 9ca8 (2510), f9b9 (2504).\nSTILL IN CI: 2505, 2506 at ps4 (the docs I had to write for their unmet documentation ACs)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788341958882937001,"uuid":"136c25bd-fb5a-4518-9852-2d7e110ec96a"}